# Bigint comparison ordering

Compares values one past the 128-bit boundaries to verify the equality
and ordering relations hold at magnitudes beyond fixed-width integers.
Every operand is bigint: comparisons are only defined between equal
types.

>>> source
low: bigint = -170141183460469231731687303715884105729
high: bigint = 170141183460469231731687303715884105728
same: bigint = 170141183460469231731687303715884105728

// Verifies the equality family on equal and distinct operands.
print(high == same)
print(low == high)

// Verifies the ordering family across the 128-bit boundaries.
print(low < high)
print(high < low)
print(high >= same)
print(low >= high)

<<< stdout
true
false
true
false
true
false

<<< stderr
